WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.520
Our master...

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:44.200
Now that we have lost the two 
Peacemakers Galil and Steyr,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:48.420
the likelihood of our being able to 
eliminate the Providence Breaker is slim.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.500
As such, I hereby request 
authorization for the use

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.860
of class one divine 
punishment configurations.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.910
I cannot condone the use of class one 
configurations within the atmosphere.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:04.890
You are authorized to continue using 
only your class two configurations.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.500
Understood.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:20.360
"A Rondo that Transcends Time"

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.930
Fafal, once you're done, go stand guard.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:37.720
Sure thing.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.220
Any luck?

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.310
I'm still not sensing anything in the 
area that could be the Royal Forces.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.300
That's good.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.980
What's with this hippo?

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.980
He's a dragon. His name is Mr. Soopie.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.440
Don't you think he reeks a bit?

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.280
Nope, not at all.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.280
You help out, too, Pacifica. 
Stop sitting around,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.870
and go fetch some water or something.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.830
It's just like camping out...

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.240
You realize that we're fugitives, right?

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.250
Good work. I feel better knowing 
that you're here, Eirote.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.210
The damage is worse than I thought...

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.640
We'll be fighting the Peacemakers 
and the Royal Forces again soon.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.180
Work up a damage report, and tell me 
how long they'll take to regenerate.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.180
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.230
You still haven't found her?

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.190
Send out the whole army, just find her!

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.110
But General,

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:39.240
we still have reconstruction and 
search and rescue operations to...

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.820
We can worry about that later.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.300
Right now, we have to hand over 
that girl to the Peacemakers.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.540
Prince Forsyth, I've brought you your meal.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.210
Oh. Thank you.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.340
How are things in the capital?

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.090
I've heard that reconstruction 
work has started.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.720
They're repairing the castle, too, but...

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.180
Well...

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.850
His Majesty is still missing.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.140
I see.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.040
And my sister? The Scrapped Princess?

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.360
Apparently, they're pursuing her.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.950
I see...

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.000
So, she's still alive.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.820
It's ready!

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.290
Make sure you load up your plates, okay?

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.330
Where are Senes and her people?

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.660
They said they'd eat at their camp.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.620
Wanna join us, Zefiris?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.090
I'm a weapon system, so 
I think I will abstain.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.990
Yeah, so?

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.550
Stop lurking back there and join us, Zefy.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:51.470
Here!

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:53.560
It's the thought that counts.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.520
Yes, sir.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:00.270
I never thought I'd be eating a meal 
cooked by the Scrapped Princess.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.730
Let's dig in!

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.410
Good grief...

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.660
Unbelievable...

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.870
Her poison's gonna destroy my stomach 
before it destroys the world...

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.830
We should've warned you.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.240
We're so sorry.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.460
Nonsense! It's delicious!

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.300
Excuse me, mine is ready, too.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.180
This is great!

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.350
Isn't this delicious? This is so good!

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.930
This is great!

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.350
We already heard you.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.560
I think I'm about to puke...

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:36.930
Um...

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.230
Have some, too, Chris.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.070
Thanks.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.910
You people don't have the gene.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.410
The Guardian gene.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:58.920
Chin?

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.000
Gene.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.630
Something that was seeded across the world

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.630
in order to protect the Providence Breaker.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.720
Apparently, Raquel and I both have it.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.900
Leo and Winia, too.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.680
We're here because we want to be here.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.180
We don't have anywhere to go back to now.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.650
Nobody told us to come here.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:23.980
I hope more people start to think like them.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:27.610
Still... I guess it's my fault.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:31.500
If you guys hadn't met me, you...

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.080
wouldn't be eating this lousy food right now.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.330
So we're back on that, are we?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.080
That's the pressing reality right now.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.450
Oh, what do you know?!

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.540
You wouldn't know good cooking if it bit you!

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.540
Now, now...

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:50.010
Still, being able to eat 
with everybody like this...

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.430
It makes me happy.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.970
It makes me happy.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.480
Oh, this feels great...

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.440
Are your feet hurting you?

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.700
Shall I make some Mr. Soopies 
to massage them for you?

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:10.450
Pass.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:11.920
Really?

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.410
I've put out a blanket for you.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:16.450
Thanks.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:19.760
What?

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:22.880
Thank you.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:24.670
I heard you the first time.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.040
No, not for that.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.740
I mean for coming all this way.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:31.510
I'm sorry I got you mixed up in all this.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.590
That's okay.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.800
I mean, I came here because I wanted to.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:40.640
And you're not the only 
reason I'm here, Pacifica.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:42.690
It's nothing.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.400
What is it? Is there something else?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.230
I said it's nothing.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.650
Huh? How come you're blushing?

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.110
C'mon, why?

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.070
Pacifica, how long are you 
going to keep wearing that?

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.250
Why don't you get changed?

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.330
But I don't have anything to change into.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.830
I said that your outfit is 
in Shannon's tent, didn't I?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:01.660
Oh, you did?

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.400
Goodnight.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.130
You don't want to sleep 
in the same tent as me?

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.070
I can't say I'm thrilled about it.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.130
Besides, that thing stinks.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.350
But I can't get to sleep 
if I'm not wearing this...

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.100
Shannon, I need my change of clothes.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.060
Thanks, good night.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:28.820
What's wrong?

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.090
Nothing. I just thought it might 
be nice to sleep beneath the stars.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.470
That might be nice.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:41.090
All those lights up there...

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.580
What do you suppose they are?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.180
I don't know.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.460
Leo, they say that long ago,

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.920
humans used to go up there.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.550
To the stars? You're pulling my leg.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.100
No, honest!

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.640
I wonder what they did up there.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.700
What the heck is this?

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:17.990
Huh?

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.070
What is that thing?

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.020
Miss Pacifica?

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.720
I wonder what I'm crying for.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:30.040
That's really weird.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.460
Why am I...?

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.420
What's the matter?

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:35.670
I don't know. But I can't...

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.910
Why am I crying?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.890
I'm sorry, Miss Pacifica!

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.020
For what? Why are you apologizing?

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.520
Well, you're...

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.860
No, I'm not crying because of you.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.110
What are you doing?

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:45.990
Socom.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.140
I petitioned our master,

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:50.860
but she denied our use of 
class one configurations.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.840
There is one thing that bothers me.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:55.960
It's about the Providence Breaker.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:57.880
What?

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:01.090
I understand the reasoning behind 
why we must eliminate her

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:05.680
as a disruptive element in order to 
stabilize the fundamental principles system.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.360
But as weapons go,

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:10.070
doesn't she seem somewhat passive to you?

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.610
I admit, she doesn't seem to possess 
any offensive capabilities.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:18.030
Is there something else?

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.780
I don't understand...

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:26.830
Is Pacifica Cassul really someone 
that we must obliterate?

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.360
Don't trouble yourself.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:32.040
It isn't our place to make those decisions.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.670
Steyr told me of the circumstances 
surrounding your decompression.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.590
If this is going to cause 
you to hesitate in combat,

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.050
request a memory wipe treatment.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.740
It will take only seconds.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.560
I don't need your concern.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:51.020
I have doubts as to the chances of our 
success now that we are unable to use

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:53.020
our class one divine 
punishment configurations.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:56.870
Perhaps I should follow Steyr's example 
and use a more underhanded approach.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.910
Isn't this a beautiful day?

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:20.840
Oh, my.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:22.840
Eirote?

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.300
Makarov!

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.140
Good afternoon.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.300
Makarov!

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.060
You brought him all this 
way for me? Thank you!

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.140
Don't mention it.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:31.770
How are the Gigases coming?

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.770
They should be repaired 
in another two days or so.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.980
I just hope we aren't found here before then.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:41.780
Dennis and Sutton are out reconnoitering 
the capital and the holy city.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:42.900
Who are you?

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.530
Christopher, former member of the 
Royal Forces Special Ops unit...

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.700
Princess Senes Lur Giat.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.040
Oh, Special Forces, huh?

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:52.000
That's reassuring, right, Eirote?

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.000
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.290
I hate to put you to work right 
away, but perhaps we should

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.880
work out a plan for when 
this site is attacked.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:58.670
That's a good idea.

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:05.240
Pacifica. Do the laundry, okay?

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.460
I'm sorry,

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:10.060
but could I trouble you to wash this, too?

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.310
Oh, I'll see to that one!

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:17.400
Time for laundry!

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:18.270
I gotta help, too?!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.690
You don't have any more itchy spots, do you?

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:28.700
We used to do laundry like this back 
in Manurhin all the time, didn't we?

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:29.660
What do you mean, "we"?

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:31.870
What's wrong, Shannon?

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.370
This stain won't come out.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:34.830
Who cares about a stain or two?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.210
I do!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.080
Here, hang these up.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.380
Now look here, kid...

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.920
Besides, I wanna take a dip.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:42.750
I mean, it's been forever 
since I last had a bath.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.210
Put up with it.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.720
C'mon, let me wash myself, too!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.680
I'll use an illusion spell to hide you, then.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.430
Thanks.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.320
Must be imagining things...

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.240
Who are you?

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.000
Isn't this a beautiful day?

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.170
Yes, it is.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:18.740
Um, if you're going for a 
swim, feel free to go first.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:21.920
Tell me.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:22.710
Excuse me?

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:28.150
Does the caged bird truly long for the sky?

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.740
Hang those up properly, you hear?

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:34.640
Sure, sure...

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:38.980
Three days to go...

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:42.610
Three days until Pacifica's 16th birthday.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.570
I wonder what'll happen.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.960
Even if we manage to protect 
Pacifica until then,

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:51.410
what'll happen afterwards?

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:54.500
No one knows that, right?

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:03.490
I guess our names might go 
down in history as traitors.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.940
Traitors who sacrificed humanity 
to protect their little sister.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.550
You're overthinking things, Shannon.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:18.020
It's a beautiful day, the 
breeze feels wonderful,

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:20.480
our laundry is nice and white...

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:26.120
I just can't bring myself to believe that 
this world will simply be destroyed.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:34.450
That optimism of yours always 
manages to cheer me up.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:42.040
Um... What are you talking about?

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.840
Would you listen to my story?

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:48.920
It's a story of the distant, distant past.

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:53.840
Humanity had created wings that let 
them soar higher than the birds.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.060
They took flight and left, 
aiming for the stars.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:02.520
But God frowned upon this.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.320
Left to its own devices,

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:11.030
humanity may have devoured 
the stars themselves.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:15.870
For that reason, and because humanity was 
a ferocious bird that killed its own kind,

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.790
God tried to capture humanity 
in order to preserve it.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.070
By putting it in a cage.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.970
But humanity fought back against God.

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:33.760
Many of those who resisted died.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:39.580
I thought to myself, if this goes on, 
all of humanity might go extinct.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:45.930
And so, I helped put humanity in its cage.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.820
They were caged,

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:54.670
but we took precautions to ensure 
that they wouldn't notice.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.970
Because if you don't know 
that there is a sky outside,

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:01.580
the cage is all there is of the world.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:02.790
Even so...

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:07.750
What do you think?

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:11.080
Do you want to leave your cage?

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.990
What do I think?

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.060
I want you to tell me.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:25.340
Tell me, Providence Breaker.

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:33.970
Big brother!

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:36.570
Pacifica!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.070
What's wrong?!

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:40.620
Miss Pacifica?

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:41.830
What happened?

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.910
Just now, a woman was...

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.250
What woman?

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.790
There's no one here...

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.540
Didn't you see her? She was right here!

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:50.440
There was a strange woman!

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:53.890
This one?

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:56.010
No, not me! That's not funny!

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:57.720
Can you describe her?

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.420
She looked just like me.

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:00.470
She was really pretty.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.720
You're talking nonsense, kid.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.180
It isn't nonsense!

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:08.140
She called me the Providence Breaker.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.860
Okay, I believe you. Wait a minute.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:12.860
Hey, Zefy.

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:14.780
Did you see her?

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.570
No, I couldn't see anything.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:20.320
It was as if the area 
was swallowed up by fog.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.940
So I was the only one who saw her?

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.160
A ghost?

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:28.040
I've never seen one of the 
entities that you call ghosts...

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.360
Still, it's good that you're safe.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:36.460
What is it?

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:39.470
No, it's nothing.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:50.400
It won't be long before everyone 
will come to kill you.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.190
And then, this world will be...

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:09.710
Merely praying will solve nothing.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.670
The Scrapped Princess' 
birthday is in three days.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:13.710
Yes, lord...

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.960
There is still something that you must do.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.050
Lord? What would you have me do?

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.930
Steyr used to tell me something.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:26.070
That it is dread and fear 
that drives humanity.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:47.450
It looks like the Scrapped Princess

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.660
fled towards the holy city via 
the underground waterways.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.000
The ones who guided her out were...

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.710
We should go, too.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:01.800
Ow!

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.070
Are you okay?

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:04.750
That's what you get for not paying attention.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:08.190
You should learn from Leo.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.440
Wow, your training is really paying off.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.560
I sort of get the feeling that I'm 
not putting it to the proper use...

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.740
The Royal Forces are 
marching in this direction.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:25.660
It doesn't look like they have 
a fix on our position yet,

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.890
but we don't have much time.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:40.110
I wonder if that lady was 
talking about this world.

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:46.020
I mean, they did say that 
our world is sealed off...

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:48.970
Pacifica.

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.160
Right, right...

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.400
The clouds are so high up...

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:37.190
Pacifica greets the day before 
her birthday in a camp site

00:22:37.190 --> 00:22:38.960
surrounded by the Royal 
Forces' giant tank squadron.

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:41.880
When she does laundry with Winia at the 
nearby river after eating breakfast,

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:44.300
she is scolded by Senes for 
not being cautious enough.

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:46.460
But that isn't the first time 
this has happened, now is it?

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:48.040
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:49.340
"Oratorio of the Mortals."

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
